PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":4,"theme":"Amazing Animals","essential_question":"What makes each animal special?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1","title":"It Has a Long Neck: have and has","objectives":["Students will be able to use have with I, you, we, they and has with he, she, it.","Students will be able to describe animals' body parts with have/has.","I can say \"I have a pet\" and \"It has a long tail\".","I can describe an animal with have and has."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام have مع I وyou وwe وthey وhas مع he وshe وit.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف أجزاء أجسام الحيوانات باستخدام have/has.","أستطيع أن أقول I have a pet وIt has a long tail.","أستطيع أن أصف حيوانًا باستخدام have وhas."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camel","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæməl/","definition":"a big desert animal with a hump on its back","arabic":"جمل","example":"The camel walks across the sand.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"lion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlaɪən/","definition":"a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head","arabic":"أسد","example":"The lion sleeps under a tree.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"elephant","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛləfənt/","definition":"a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)","arabic":"فيل","example":"An elephant drinks with its trunk.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"giraffe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒɚˈæf/","definition":"a very tall animal with a long neck","arabic":"زرافة","example":"The giraffe eats leaves from tall trees.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use have and has to say what someone owns or what body parts an animal has.\nUse has with he, she, it and one person or animal: A camel has a hump. Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals: Birds have wings.\nI / you / we / they → have: I have a cat.\nhe / she / it / one person or animal → has: It has a long tail.\nplural nouns → have: Rabbits have long ears.","examples":["I have two goldfish.","A lion has sharp teeth.","We have a cat at home.","Turtles have hard shells.","My cousin has a horse.","You have a beautiful parrot!","The elephant has big ears.","Giraffes have long necks."],"common_errors":["✗ The camel have a hump. → ✓ The camel has a hump. (One animal (it) → has.)","✗ He has a cat and he have a dog. → ✓ He has a cat and a dog. (he → has every time.)","✗ Rabbit has long ears. → ✓ A rabbit has long ears. / Rabbits have long ears. (Use a for one, or the plural for all rabbits.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع، وhas مع he وshe وit والمفرد.\nفي العربية نقول «للجمل سنام» أو «عنده»، وفي الإنجليزية: The camel has a hump.\nلا تنسَ a مع المفرد: A rabbit has long ears، أو استخدم الجمع: Rabbits have long ears."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Has a Long Neck: have and has”. Let’s learn have / has together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U4-LS1 | It Has a Long Neck: have and has","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Lina's Animal Book”: I am Lina. I have a big book about animals. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"I am Lina. I have a big book about animals.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use have and has to say what someone owns or what body parts an animal has. Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal: A camel has a hump. Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals: Birds have wings.","on_screen":"I / you / we / they → have: I have a cat. • he / she / it / one person or animal → has: It has a long tail. • plural nouns → have: Rabbits have long ears.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I have two goldfish. A lion has sharp teeth. We have a cat at home.","on_screen":"I have two goldfish. / A lion has sharp teeth. / We have a cat at home.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The camel have a hump.” That’s not right. We say: “The camel has a hump.” One animal (it) → has.","on_screen":"✗ The camel have a hump.   ✓ The camel has a hump.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"A giraffe ___ a long neck.\" One animal or many? have or has? … Think! … One animal – *has*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I have a pet\" and \"It has a long tail\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I have a pet\" and \"It has a long tail\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: have / has.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع، وhas مع he وshe وit والمفرد.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The camel have a hump. — الصحيح: The camel has a hump.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I have a pet وIt has a long tail."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Lina's Animal Book","body":"I am Lina. I have a big book about animals.\nLook at page one! A camel has a long neck and a hump. It has big feet for the sand.\nA parrot has two wings and a strong beak. It has red and green feathers.\nI have a pet rabbit. My rabbit has long ears and soft white fur.\nMy brothers have a turtle. It has a hard shell.\nWe all love animals!","word_count":73,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"A lion ___ a big mane.","options":["have","has","is","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"I ___ a little brother.","options":["am","has","have","is"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"Elephants ___ long trunks.","options":["have","has","is","am"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"My aunt ___ a white cat.","options":["are","have","is","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"We ___ a garden with a lemon tree.","options":["am","has","is","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"The parrot ___ green feathers.","options":["have","am","has","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write have or has. Word bank: has, have","items":[{"q":"A turtle ______ a hard shell.","options":[],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"You ______ a nice smile.","options":[],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"Camels ______ humps on their backs.","options":[],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"has / long / The / rabbit / ears   ( . )","options":["has","long","The","rabbit","ears"],"answer":"The rabbit has long ears.","explanation":"Word order: Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"ponies / They / two / have   ( . )","options":["ponies","They","two","have"],"answer":"They have two ponies.","explanation":"Word order: Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"tail / My / has / short / a / dog   ( . )","options":["tail","My","has","short","a","dog"],"answer":"My dog has a short tail.","explanation":"Word order: Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about animals you know.","items":[{"q":"A cat has ___.","options":[],"answer":"A cat has soft fur.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Birds have ___.","options":[],"answer":"Birds have two wings.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have ___ at home.","options":[],"answer":"I have a goldfish at home.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My friend has ___.","options":[],"answer":"My friend has a bike.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A camel has ___.","options":[],"answer":"A camel has a hump.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Draw and write.","items":[{"q":"Draw a pet you have or want. Write 3 sentences with has.","options":[],"answer":"My cat is gray. It has green eyes. It has a long tail.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what your family has.","options":[],"answer":"We have a big car. My sister has a canary.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a mystery animal with has. Your partner guesses.","options":[],"answer":"It has a long neck. It has four legs. (a giraffe)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have / has correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using have / has without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"a camel"},{"label":"a parrot"},{"label":"my cat"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"elephants"},{"label":"my brother"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A horse ___ four legs.","options":["have","has","is","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"They ___ a new puppy.","options":["is","are","have","has"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"My uncle ___ a farm.","options":["are","am","has","have"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"Owls ___ big eyes.","options":["has","is","am","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"You ___ a lovely garden.","options":["am","is","has","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"","options":["The bird has a red beak.","The bird is a red beak.","The bird have a red beak.","The bird has red beak a."],"answer":"The bird has a red beak.","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"My sister and I ___ a rabbit.","options":["have","am","has","is"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"","options":["Zebra has black and white stripes.","A zebra has black and white stripes.","A zebra are black and white stripes.","A zebra have black and white stripes."],"answer":"A zebra has black and white stripes.","explanation":"Use a/an with one animal.","explanation_ar":"استخدم a/an مع المفرد."},{"q":"It ___ big ears and a long trunk.","options":["have","is","are","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"","options":["My grandpa is two camels.","My grandpa has two camel.","My grandpa has two camels.","My grandpa have two camels."],"answer":"My grandpa has two camels.","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Lina sitting on a rug reading a big animal book with pictures of a camel, a parrot and a giraffe; her white rabbit beside her. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina sitting on a rug reading a big animal book with pictures of a camel, a parrot and a giraffe; her white rabbit beside her"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about have / has, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about have / has, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows camel (a big desert animal with a hump on its back); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing camel: a big desert animal with a hump on its back"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lion (a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lion: a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows elephant (a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing elephant: a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows giraffe (a very tall animal with a long neck); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing giraffe: a very tall animal with a long neck"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W01","script":"camel. camel. The camel walks across the sand.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W02","script":"lion. lion. The lion sleeps under a tree.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W03","script":"elephant. elephant. An elephant drinks with its trunk.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-W04","script":"giraffe. giraffe. The giraffe eats leaves from tall trees.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-T1","script":"I am Lina. I have a big book about animals. Look at page one! A camel has a long neck and a hump. It has big feet for the sand. A parrot has two wings and a strong beak. It has red and green feathers. I have a pet rabbit. My rabbit has long ears and soft white fur. My brothers have a turtle. It has a hard shell. We all love animals!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Has a Long Neck: have and has”. Let’s learn have / has together. Listen to the start of “Lina's Animal Book”: I am Lina. I have a big book about animals. Look at the green words. We use have and has to say what someone owns or what body parts an animal has. Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal: A camel has a hump. Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals: Birds have wings. Here are some examples. I have two goldfish. A lion has sharp teeth. We have a cat at home. Be careful! Some learners say: “The camel have a hump.” That’s not right. We say: “The camel has a hump.” One animal (it) → has. Quick check: \"A giraffe ___ a long neck.\" One animal or many? have or has? … Think! … One animal – *has*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I have a pet\" and \"It has a long tail\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2","title":"A Tall Giraffe: Adjectives and don't/doesn't have","objectives":["Students will be able to put adjectives before nouns (a tall giraffe).","Students will be able to make negatives and questions with don't/doesn't have and Do/Does … have…?","I can say \"a big gray elephant\".","I can say \"It doesn't have a tail\" and ask \"Does it have fur?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع الصفة قبل الاسم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من النفي والسؤال باستخدام don't/doesn't have وDo/Does … have…؟","أستطيع أن أقول a big gray elephant.","أستطيع أن أقول It doesn't have a tail وأسأل Does it have fur?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rabbit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈræbət/","definition":"a small animal with long ears and soft fur","arabic":"أرنب","example":"My rabbit loves carrots.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"turtle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɝtəl/","definition":"an animal with a hard shell on its back","arabic":"سلحفاة","example":"The turtle swims in the pond.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"parrot","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛrət/","definition":"a colorful bird that can copy words","arabic":"ببغاء","example":"Our parrot says \"Hello!\"","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"tail","pos":"noun","ipa":"/teɪl/","definition":"the long part at the back of an animal's body","arabic":"ذيل","example":"The dog wags its tail.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Adjectives describe nouns: big, small, long, short, soft, tall. In English the adjective comes before the noun: a tall giraffe (NOT a giraffe tall).\nAdjectives never take -s: long ears (NOT longs ears).\nNegative: I/you/we/they don't have; he/she/it doesn't have. Questions: Do you have…? / Does it have…? After doesn't and does, use have (not has).","examples":["A cheetah is a fast animal.","My cat has green eyes.","Snakes don't have legs.","A rabbit doesn't have a long tail.","Do you have a hamster? – No, I don't.","Does a camel have a hump? – Yes, it does.","The little chick has yellow feathers.","We don't have a garden."],"common_errors":["✗ a cat black → ✓ a black cat (The adjective comes before the noun.)","✗ It doesn't has wings. → ✓ It doesn't have wings. (After doesn't, use have.)","✗ You have a pet? → ✓ Do you have a pet? (Questions with have need Do/Does.)","✗ two bigs dogs → ✓ two big dogs (Adjectives never take -s.)"],"arabic":"في الإنجليزية الصفة تأتي قبل الاسم: a black cat (قطة سوداء).\nالصفة لا تُجمع: big dogs وليس bigs dogs.\nالنفي: don't have مع I وyou وwe وthey، وdoesn't have مع he وshe وit.\nالسؤال: Do you have…? / Does it have…? وبعد does وdoesn't نستخدم have وليس has."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Tall Giraffe: Adjectives and don't/doesn't have”. Let’s learn adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U4-LS2 | A Tall Giraffe: Adjectives and don't/doesn't have","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: It has a long tail. • They have big ears. I don't have a cat. • A fish doesn't have legs. Do you have a pet? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • Does it have fur? – Yes, it does. / No, it doesn't.","on_screen":"It has a long tail. • They have big ears. | I don't have a cat. • A fish doesn't have legs. | Do you have a pet? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • Does it have fur? – Yes, it does. / No, it doesn't.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Adjectives describe nouns: big, small, long, short, soft, tall. In English the adjective comes before the noun: a tall giraffe (NOT a giraffe tall). Adjectives never take -s: long ears (NOT longs ears).","on_screen":"adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. A cheetah is a fast animal. My cat has green eyes. Snakes don't have legs.","on_screen":"A cheetah is a fast animal. / My cat has green eyes. / Snakes don't have legs.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “a cat black.” That’s not right. We say: “a black cat.” The adjective comes before the noun.","on_screen":"✗ a cat black   ✓ a black cat","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"a giraffe tall\" or \"a tall giraffe\"? … Think! … *a tall giraffe* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a big gray elephant\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"a big gray elephant\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في الإنجليزية الصفة تأتي قبل الاسم: a black cat (قطة سوداء).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: a cat black — الصحيح: a black cat","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول a big gray elephant."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Look at that ___.","options":["tall giraffes a","giraffe tall","tall giraffe","talls giraffe"],"answer":"tall giraffe","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"A fish ___ legs.","options":["doesn't has","don't have","not have","doesn't have"],"answer":"doesn't have","explanation":"he, she, it → doesn't have (not has).","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't have."},{"q":"We ___ a pet at home.","options":["don't have","doesn't have","don't has","not have"],"answer":"don't have","explanation":"I, you, we, they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't have."},{"q":"___ you have a bike?","options":["Does","Are","Do","Is"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"___ the parrot have a red beak?","options":["Has","Does","Do","Is"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"Does a turtle have a shell? – Yes, it ___.","options":["has","does","is","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make the sentences negative.","items":[{"q":"I have a hamster.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"I don't have a hamster.","explanation":"I, you, we, they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't have."},{"q":"The snake has legs.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"The snake doesn't have legs.","explanation":"he, she, it → doesn't have (not has).","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't have."},{"q":"My friends have a horse.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"My friends don't have a horse.","explanation":"I, you, we, they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't have."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the adjective in the right place.","items":[{"q":"a cat (gray)  (add the adjective)","options":[],"answer":"a gray cat","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"two dogs (small)  (add the adjective)","options":[],"answer":"two small dogs","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"a beak (sharp)  (add the adjective)","options":[],"answer":"a sharp beak","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about you. Use short answers.","items":[{"q":"Do you have a pet?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I do. / No, I don't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Does your house have a garden?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, it does. / No, it doesn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do your cousins have a cat?","options":[],"answer":"No, they don't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Does your best friend have a brother?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he does.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you have a big family?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I do.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Play \"Guess the Animal\".","items":[{"q":"Think of an animal. Write 3 sentences: 2 with has and 1 with doesn't have.","options":[],"answer":"It has gray skin. It has a long trunk. It doesn't have fur. (an elephant)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 Does it have…? questions to ask your partner.","options":[],"answer":"Does it have wings? Does it have four legs? Does it have a long tail?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe your favorite animal with 3 adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"A lion is big, strong and brave.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…?.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"a lion / sharp teeth / +"},{"cue":"a turtle / wings / –"},{"cue":"you / a pet / ?"},{"cue":"a giraffe / a long neck / +"},{"cue":"I / a horse / –"},{"cue":"a parrot / a beak / ?"},{"cue":"my sister / a rabbit / +"},{"cue":"fish / legs / –"},{"cue":"elephants / big ears / ?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A penguin has ___.","options":["shorts wings","short wings","wing short","wings short"],"answer":"short wings","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"My grandparents ___ a computer.","options":["don't have","not have","don't has","doesn't have"],"answer":"don't have","explanation":"I, you, we, they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't have."},{"q":"A worm ___ legs.","options":["doesn't have","doesn't has","don't have","hasn't"],"answer":"doesn't have","explanation":"he, she, it → doesn't have (not has).","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't have."},{"q":"___ your cat have blue eyes?","options":["Has","Is","Does","Do"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"Do you have a sister? – No, I ___.","options":["doesn't","don't","haven't","am not"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"","options":["I have two smalls fish.","I have two fish small.","I have small two fish.","I have two small fish."],"answer":"I have two small fish.","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"","options":["It doesn't have a tail.","It not have a tail.","It don't have a tail.","It doesn't has a tail."],"answer":"It doesn't have a tail.","explanation":"he, she, it → doesn't have (not has).","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't have."},{"q":"","options":["Do they has a farm?","Does they have a farm?","Do they have a farm?","They have a farm?"],"answer":"Do they have a farm?","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"Does the owl have big eyes? – ___","options":["Yes, it has.","Yes, does it.","Yes, it do.","Yes, it does."],"answer":"Yes, it does.","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"","options":["We have a blacks and whites cat.","We has a black and white cat.","We have a black and white cat.","We have a cat black and white."],"answer":"We have a black and white cat.","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf and Adam playing a guessing game at the zoo fence, one boy asking \"Does it have stripes?\" while a zebra stands behind them. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf and Adam playing a guessing game at the zoo fence, one boy asking \"Does it have stripes?\" while a zebra stands behind them"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Amazing Animals”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of adjectives before nouns"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rabbit (a small animal with long ears and soft fur); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rabbit: a small animal with long ears and soft fur"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows turtle (an animal with a hard shell on its back); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing turtle: an animal with a hard shell on its back"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows parrot (a colorful bird that can copy words); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing parrot: a colorful bird that can copy words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tail (the long part at the back of an animal's body); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tail: the long part at the back of an animal's body"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W01","script":"rabbit. rabbit. My rabbit loves carrots.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W02","script":"turtle. turtle. The turtle swims in the pond.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W03","script":"parrot. parrot. Our parrot says \"Hello!\"","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-W04","script":"tail. tail. The dog wags its tail.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Tall Giraffe: Adjectives and don't/doesn't have”. Let’s learn adjectives before nouns; don't/doesn't have; Do/Does … have…? together. Remember these patterns: It has a long tail. • They have big ears. I don't have a cat. • A fish doesn't have legs. Do you have a pet? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • Does it have fur? – Yes, it does. / No, it doesn't. Adjectives describe nouns: big, small, long, short, soft, tall. In English the adjective comes before the noun: a tall giraffe (NOT a giraffe tall). Adjectives never take -s: long ears (NOT longs ears). Here are some examples. A cheetah is a fast animal. My cat has green eyes. Snakes don't have legs. Be careful! Some learners say: “a cat black.” That’s not right. We say: “a black cat.” The adjective comes before the noun. Quick check: \"a giraffe tall\" or \"a tall giraffe\"? … Think! … *a tall giraffe* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a big gray elephant\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3","title":"Animal Words: Huge, Tiny and More","objectives":["Students will be able to name animals and their body parts.","Students will be able to choose between big/huge and small/tiny to show shades of meaning.","I can name animals and their body parts.","I can say if an animal is big, huge, small or tiny."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية الحيوانات وأجزاء أجسامها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين big/huge وsmall/tiny لإظهار درجات المعنى.","أستطيع أن أسمّي الحيوانات وأجزاء أجسامها.","أستطيع أن أقول إن الحيوان big أو huge أو small أو tiny."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"wing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɪŋ/","definition":"the part of a bird's body it uses to fly","arabic":"جناح","example":"The falcon opens its wings.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"fur","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɝ/","definition":"the soft hair on some animals","arabic":"فرو","example":"The kitten has soft gray fur.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"neck","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nɛk/","definition":"the part of the body between the head and the body","arabic":"رقبة","example":"A swan has a long white neck.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"shell","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃɛl/","definition":"the hard outside part of some animals","arabic":"صَدَفة / درع","example":"The snail hides in its shell.","image_id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Animal words often go with body-part words: a parrot has wings and a beak; a turtle has a shell; a cat has fur and a tail.\nSome words are \"stronger\" than others. Huge means very, very big. Tiny means very, very small. We call this shades of meaning.\nGroup words to remember them: animals with fur, animals with wings, animals with shells.\nCollocations/phrases: tiny → small → big → huge | short → long • slow → fast • soft → hard | animals with wings: parrot, falcon, owl • animals with fur: rabbit, lion, camel • animals with shells: turtle, snail, crab","examples":["An ant is tiny.","A blue whale is huge.","The giraffe has a very long neck.","The turtle hides inside its shell.","The parrot flaps its wings.","My kitten's fur is fluffy.","The lion has a big golden mane.","A camel can walk for days without water."],"common_errors":["✗ The elephant is very huge. → ✓ The elephant is huge. (huge already means very big.)","✗ The bird has two hands. → ✓ The bird has two wings. (Birds have wings, not hands.)","✗ The rabbit has hair soft. → ✓ The rabbit has soft fur. (Animals have fur; the adjective comes first.)"],"arabic":"بعض الكلمات أقوى من غيرها: huge = ضخم جدًا، وtiny = صغير جدًا.\nلا نقول very huge لأن huge تعني «كبير جدًا» أصلًا.\nللحيوانات نقول fur (فرو) وwings (أجنحة) وshell (درع) وtail (ذيل)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Animal Words: Huge, Tiny and More”. Let’s learn animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U4-LS3 | Animal Words: Huge, Tiny and More","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. wing: the part of a bird's body it uses to fly. fur: the soft hair on some animals. neck: the part of the body between the head and the body.","on_screen":"wing | fur | neck","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Animal words often go with body-part words: a parrot has wings and a beak; a turtle has a shell; a cat has fur and a tail. Some words are \"stronger\" than others. Huge means very, very big. Tiny means very, very small. We call this shades of meaning.","on_screen":"animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. An ant is tiny. A blue whale is huge. The giraffe has a very long neck.","on_screen":"An ant is tiny. / A blue whale is huge. / The giraffe has a very long neck.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The elephant is very huge.” That’s not right. We say: “The elephant is huge.” huge already means very big.","on_screen":"✗ The elephant is very huge.   ✓ The elephant is huge.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which is bigger: big or huge? … Think! … *huge* Great job! Now you can say: I can name animals and their body parts.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name animals and their body parts.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعض الكلمات أقوى من غيرها: huge = ضخم جدًا، وtiny = صغير جدًا.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The elephant is very huge. — الصحيح: The elephant is huge.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي الحيوانات وأجزاء أجسامها."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"A mouse is ___. It is very, very small.","options":["tiny","long","tall","huge"],"answer":"tiny","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"An elephant is ___. It is very, very big.","options":["tiny","small","huge","short"],"answer":"huge","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A falcon flies with its ___.","options":["shell","wings","fur","tail"],"answer":"wings","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"A turtle has a hard ___.","options":["shell","fur","mane","wing"],"answer":"shell","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"This animal lives in the desert and has a hump.","options":["parrot","rabbit","turtle","camel"],"answer":"camel","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."},{"q":"This bird can copy words.","options":["giraffe","lion","camel","parrot"],"answer":"parrot","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the animal to its special body part.","items":[{"q":"giraffe","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"a very long neck","explanation":"giraffe → a very long neck. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"rabbit","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"long ears and soft fur","explanation":"rabbit → long ears and soft fur. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"elephant","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"a long trunk","explanation":"elephant → a long trunk. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"lion","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"a big golden mane","explanation":"lion → a big golden mane. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"turtle","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"a hard shell","explanation":"turtle → a hard shell. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"peacock","options":["long ears and soft fur","a big golden mane","a hard shell","a long trunk","a colorful tail","a very long neck"],"answer":"a colorful tail","explanation":"peacock → a colorful tail. tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the sentences about animals.","items":[{"q":"A ___ is tiny.","options":[],"answer":"A ladybug is tiny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A ___ is huge.","options":[],"answer":"A whale is huge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite animal has ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite animal has stripes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Animals with wings: ___, ___ and ___.","options":[],"answer":"parrot, owl and falcon","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Animals with fur: ___, ___ and ___.","options":[],"answer":"cat, rabbit and bear","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make an \"Animal Size Line\".","items":[{"q":"Draw 4 animals from tiny to huge. Label them.","options":[],"answer":"an ant (tiny), a cat (small), a horse (big), a whale (huge)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your size line.","options":[],"answer":"An ant is tiny. A horse is big. A whale is huge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a riddle about an animal for your partner.","options":[],"answer":"It is huge. It is gray. It has a trunk. What is it?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"camel","match":"a big desert animal with a hump on its back","arabic":"جمل"},{"word":"lion","match":"a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head","arabic":"أسد"},{"word":"elephant","match":"a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)","arabic":"فيل"},{"word":"giraffe","match":"a very tall animal with a long neck","arabic":"زرافة"},{"word":"rabbit","match":"a small animal with long ears and soft fur","arabic":"أرنب"},{"word":"turtle","match":"an animal with a hard shell on its back","arabic":"سلحفاة"},{"word":"parrot","match":"a colorful bird that can copy words","arabic":"ببغاء"},{"word":"tail","match":"the long part at the back of an animal's body","arabic":"ذيل"},{"word":"wing","match":"the part of a bird's body it uses to fly","arabic":"جناح"},{"word":"fur","match":"the soft hair on some animals","arabic":"فرو"},{"word":"neck","match":"the part of the body between the head and the body","arabic":"رقبة"},{"word":"shell","match":"the hard outside part of some animals","arabic":"صَدَفة / درع"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A ladybug is ___.","options":["tall","huge","heavy","tiny"],"answer":"tiny","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A dinosaur was ___.","options":["tiny","short","small","huge"],"answer":"huge","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A bird uses its ___ to fly.","options":["wings","shell","ears","tail"],"answer":"wings","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"A cat has soft ___.","options":["fur","beak","wings","shell"],"answer":"fur","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"This animal has a long trunk.","options":["rabbit","elephant","giraffe","camel"],"answer":"elephant","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."},{"q":"","options":["The whale is huge.","The whale is huges.","The whale huge is.","The whale is very huge."],"answer":"The whale is huge.","explanation":"Don't use very with huge or tiny.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم very مع huge أو tiny."},{"q":"Which word means \"very small\"?","options":["long","soft","tiny","huge"],"answer":"tiny","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A snail carries its ___ on its back.","options":["mane","shell","wings","fur"],"answer":"shell","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"This tall animal eats leaves from high trees.","options":["turtle","giraffe","rabbit","parrot"],"answer":"giraffe","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."},{"q":"Choose the correct order (small → big):","options":["small, tiny, huge, big","big, tiny, huge, small","tiny, small, big, huge","huge, big, small, tiny"],"answer":"tiny, small, big, huge","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A size line on a poster: a tiny ant, a small rabbit, a big camel and a huge elephant, Zaki the Falcon measuring with a ruler. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A size line on a poster: a tiny ant, a small rabbit, a big camel and a huge elephant, Zaki the Falcon measuring with a ruler"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wing (the part of a bird's body it uses to fly); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wing: the part of a bird's body it uses to fly"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows fur (the soft hair on some animals); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing fur: the soft hair on some animals"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows neck (the part of the body between the head and the body); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing neck: the part of the body between the head and the body"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows shell (the hard outside part of some animals); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing shell: the hard outside part of some animals"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W01","script":"wing. wing. The falcon opens its wings.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W02","script":"fur. fur. The kitten has soft gray fur.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W03","script":"neck. neck. A swan has a long white neck.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-W04","script":"shell. shell. The snail hides in its shell.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Animal Words: Huge, Tiny and More”. Let’s learn animal and body-part words; shades of meaning (big → huge, small → tiny) together. Meet some new words. wing: the part of a bird's body it uses to fly. fur: the soft hair on some animals. neck: the part of the body between the head and the body. Animal words often go with body-part words: a parrot has wings and a beak; a turtle has a shell; a cat has fur and a tail. Some words are \"stronger\" than others. Huge means very, very big. Tiny means very, very small. We call this shades of meaning. Here are some examples. An ant is tiny. A blue whale is huge. The giraffe has a very long neck. Be careful! Some learners say: “The elephant is very huge.” That’s not right. We say: “The elephant is huge.” huge already means very big. Quick check: Which is bigger: big or huge? … Think! … *huge* Great job! Now you can say: I can name animals and their body parts.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4","title":"One Fox, Two Foxes: Spelling Plurals","objectives":["Students will be able to spell plurals with -s, -es and -ies.","Students will be able to use some special plurals: mice, feet, teeth, sheep, fish.","I can spell plurals like foxes and butterflies.","I can use special plurals like mice and sheep."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة الجمع بإضافة s وes وies.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام بعض الجموع الخاصة: mice وfeet وteeth وsheep وfish.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى جموعًا مثل foxes وbutterflies.","أستطيع أن أستخدم جموعًا خاصة مثل mice وsheep."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camel","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæməl/","definition":"a big desert animal with a hump on its back","arabic":"جمل","example":"The camel walks across the sand.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlaɪən/","definition":"a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head","arabic":"أسد","example":"The lion sleeps under a tree.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"elephant","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛləfənt/","definition":"a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)","arabic":"فيل","example":"An elephant drinks with its trunk.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"giraffe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒɚˈæf/","definition":"a very tall animal with a long neck","arabic":"زرافة","example":"The giraffe eats leaves from tall trees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rabbit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈræbət/","definition":"a small animal with long ears and soft fur","arabic":"أرنب","example":"My rabbit loves carrots.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"turtle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɝtəl/","definition":"an animal with a hard shell on its back","arabic":"سلحفاة","example":"The turtle swims in the pond.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Most nouns add -s: camel → camels. Nouns ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es: fox → foxes.\nNouns ending in a consonant + y change y to i and add -es: butterfly → butterflies. But vowel + y just adds -s: monkey → monkeys.\nSome plurals are special. Learn them by heart: mouse → mice, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, sheep → sheep, fish → fish.\n+ s: tails, wings, parrots\n+ es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: buses, foxes, peaches\nconsonant + y → ies: puppy → puppies, butterfly → butterflies\nspecial: mouse → mice • foot → feet • tooth → teeth • sheep → sheep • fish → fish","examples":["The farm has ten sheep.","Two foxes live in the forest.","I can see three butterflies.","Our dog has four puppies.","Cats like to chase mice.","A camel has big feet.","The monkeys are funny.","The lion has sharp teeth."],"common_errors":["✗ two foxs → ✓ two foxes (After x, add -es.)","✗ three butterflys → ✓ three butterflies (consonant + y → ies.)","✗ many sheeps → ✓ many sheep (sheep does not change.)","✗ two mouses → ✓ two mice (mouse has a special plural.)"],"arabic":"معظم الأسماء نضيف لها s للجمع: camels.\nنضيف es بعد s وsh وch وx: foxes، وإذا انتهت الكلمة بحرف ساكن + y نحذف y ونضيف ies: butterflies.\nبعض الجموع خاصة ويجب حفظها: mice وfeet وteeth، وsheep وfish لا تتغير."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “One Fox, Two Foxes: Spelling Plurals”. Let’s learn plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U4-LS4 | One Fox, Two Foxes: Spelling Plurals","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Most nouns add -s: camel → camels. Nouns ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es: fox → foxes.","on_screen":"plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Most nouns add -s: camel → camels. Nouns ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es: fox → foxes. Nouns ending in a consonant + y change y to i and add -es: butterfly → butterflies. But vowel + y just adds -s: monkey → monkeys.","on_screen":"+ s: tails, wings, parrots • + es after s, ss, sh, ch, x: buses, foxes, peaches • consonant + y → ies: puppy → puppies, butterfly → butterflies","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The farm has ten sheep. Two foxes live in the forest. I can see three butterflies.","on_screen":"The farm has ten sheep. / Two foxes live in the forest. / I can see three butterflies.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “two foxs.” That’s not right. We say: “two foxes.” After x, add -es.","on_screen":"✗ two foxs   ✓ two foxes","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is the plural of \"sheep\" \"sheeps\"? … Think! … No – *sheep*. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell plurals like foxes and butterflies.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell plurals like foxes and butterflies.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","معظم الأسماء نضيف لها s للجمع: camels.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: two foxs — الصحيح: two foxes","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى جموعًا مثل foxes وbutterflies."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Zoo Notice (editing passage)","body":"Welcome to Taif Zoo! Today you can see two lionnes, six monkies and three foxs. The ponys are near the gate. Please do not feed the fishes.","word_count":27,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct plural.","items":[{"q":"one fox → two ___","options":["foxes","foxs","foxies","fox"],"answer":"foxes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"one puppy → three ___","options":["puppy","puppyes","puppies","puppys"],"answer":"puppies","explanation":"Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"one parrot → five ___","options":["parroties","parrotes","parrot","parrots"],"answer":"parrots","explanation":"Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"one mouse → two ___","options":["mices","mousies","mouses","mice"],"answer":"mice","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"one sheep → ten ___","options":["sheepes","sheepies","sheep","sheeps"],"answer":"sheep","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"one monkey → four ___","options":["monkies","monkeys","monkey","monkeyes"],"answer":"monkeys","explanation":"Vowel + y → just add -s (monkeys).","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y نضيف s فقط."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling mistake.","items":[{"q":"I see two butterflys in the garden.","options":[],"answer":"I see two butterflies in the garden.","explanation":"butterflys → butterflies. Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: butterflys → butterflies. حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"The lunchs are in the fridge.","options":[],"answer":"The lunches are in the fridge.","explanation":"lunchs → lunches. After s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: lunchs → lunches. بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"A horse has four foots.","options":[],"answer":"A horse has four feet.","explanation":"foots → feet. Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: foots → feet. جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"We have three kittenes.","options":[],"answer":"We have three kittens.","explanation":"kittenes → kittens. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: kittenes → kittens. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"The babys are sleeping.","options":[],"answer":"The babies are sleeping.","explanation":"babys → babies. Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: babys → babies. حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"Brush your tooths every night.","options":[],"answer":"Brush your teeth every night.","explanation":"tooths → teeth. Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: tooths → teeth. جمع خاص يُحفظ."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the zoo notice.","items":[{"q":"Today you can see two lionnes, six monkeys and three foxes.","options":[],"answer":"Today you can see two lions, six monkeys and three foxes.","explanation":"lionnes → lions. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: lionnes → lions. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"Today you can see two lions, six monkies and three foxes.","options":[],"answer":"Today you can see two lions, six monkeys and three foxes.","explanation":"monkies → monkeys. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: monkies → monkeys. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"Today you can see two lions, six monkeys and three foxs.","options":[],"answer":"Today you can see two lions, six monkeys and three foxes.","explanation":"foxs → foxes. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: foxs → foxes. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"The ponys are near the gate.","options":[],"answer":"The ponies are near the gate.","explanation":"ponys → ponies. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ponys → ponies. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"Please do not feed the fishes.","options":[],"answer":"Please do not feed the fish.","explanation":"fishes → fish. Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: fishes → fish. معظم الأسماء تضيف s."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about many animals.","items":[{"q":"Write the plurals: bus, cherry, baby, wolf? (Ask your teacher about wolf!)","options":[],"answer":"buses, cherries, babies, wolves","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a farm with plurals.","options":[],"answer":"The farm has five sheep. There are ten chickens. Two horses are in the field.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Make a spelling quiz for your partner with 3 plurals.","options":[],"answer":"puppy → puppies; box → boxes; tooth → teeth","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"camels","clue":""},{"word":"foxes","clue":""},{"word":"butterflies","clue":""},{"word":"puppies","clue":""},{"word":"mice","clue":""},{"word":"sheep","clue":""},{"word":"teeth","clue":""},{"word":"wings","clue":""},{"word":"turtles","clue":""},{"word":"monkeys","clue":""},{"word":"camel","clue":"a big desert animal with a hump on its back"},{"word":"lion","clue":"a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"one box → two ___","options":["boxs","box","boxes","boxies"],"answer":"boxes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"one butterfly → many ___","options":["butterflies","butterflys","butterflyes","butterfly"],"answer":"butterflies","explanation":"Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"one tooth → two ___","options":["teeths","teeth","toothes","tooths"],"answer":"teeth","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"one turtle → three ___","options":["turtlees","turtlies","turtles","turtle"],"answer":"turtles","explanation":"Most nouns add -s.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأسماء تضيف s."},{"q":"one donkey → two ___","options":["donkeyes","donkeys","donkies","donkey"],"answer":"donkeys","explanation":"Vowel + y → just add -s (monkeys).","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y نضيف s فقط."},{"q":"","options":["Three sheep is in the field.","Three sheep are in the field.","Three sheepes are in the field.","Three sheeps are in the field."],"answer":"Three sheep are in the field.","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"one peach → four ___","options":["peachs","peach","peachies","peaches"],"answer":"peaches","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"","options":["The cat chases two mice.","The cat chases two mouse.","The cat chases two mices.","The cat chases two mouses."],"answer":"The cat chases two mice.","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"Which plural is spelled correctly?","options":["ladys","ladyes","ladies","ladis"],"answer":"ladies","explanation":"Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"one foot → two ___","options":["foots","feets","footes","feet"],"answer":"feet","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Amazing Animals” that shows plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Amazing Animals” that shows plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “One Fox, Two Foxes: Spelling Plurals”. Let’s learn plural spelling: -s, -es, -ies and some special plurals together. Most nouns add -s: camel → camels. Nouns ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es: fox → foxes. Most nouns add -s: camel → camels. Nouns ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es: fox → foxes. Nouns ending in a consonant + y change y to i and add -es: butterfly → butterflies. But vowel + y just adds -s: monkey → monkeys. Here are some examples. The farm has ten sheep. Two foxes live in the forest. I can see three butterflies. Be careful! Some learners say: “two foxs.” That’s not right. We say: “two foxes.” After x, add -es. Quick check: Is the plural of \"sheep\" \"sheeps\"? … Think! … No – *sheep*. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell plurals like foxes and butterflies.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5","title":"Animal Fact File: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to describe an animal using have/has and adjectives.","Students will be able to write a short animal fact file with correct plurals and punctuation.","I can describe an animal to my class.","I can write an animal fact file."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف حيوان باستخدام have/has والصفات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة ملف حقائق قصير عن حيوان بجمع وترقيم صحيحين.","أستطيع أن أصف حيوانًا لزملائي.","أستطيع أن أكتب ملف حقائق عن حيوان."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camel","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæməl/","definition":"a big desert animal with a hump on its back","arabic":"جمل","example":"The camel walks across the sand.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlaɪən/","definition":"a big wild cat; the male has lots of hair on its head","arabic":"أسد","example":"The lion sleeps under a tree.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"elephant","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛləfənt/","definition":"a very big gray animal with a long nose (a trunk)","arabic":"فيل","example":"An elephant drinks with its trunk.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"giraffe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒɚˈæf/","definition":"a very tall animal with a long neck","arabic":"زرافة","example":"The giraffe eats leaves from tall trees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rabbit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈræbət/","definition":"a small animal with long ears and soft fur","arabic":"أرنب","example":"My rabbit loves carrots.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"turtle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɝtəl/","definition":"an animal with a hard shell on its back","arabic":"سلحفاة","example":"The turtle swims in the pond.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"parrot","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛrət/","definition":"a colorful bird that can copy words","arabic":"ببغاء","example":"Our parrot says \"Hello!\"","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tail","pos":"noun","ipa":"/teɪl/","definition":"the long part at the back of an animal's body","arabic":"ذيل","example":"The dog wags its tail.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɪŋ/","definition":"the part of a bird's body it uses to fly","arabic":"جناح","example":"The falcon opens its wings.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fur","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɝ/","definition":"the soft hair on some animals","arabic":"فرو","example":"The kitten has soft gray fur.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"neck","pos":"noun","ipa":"/nɛk/","definition":"the part of the body between the head and the body","arabic":"رقبة","example":"A swan has a long white neck.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shell","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃɛl/","definition":"the hard outside part of some animals","arabic":"صَدَفة / درع","example":"The snail hides in its shell.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: have/has, don't/doesn't have, adjectives before nouns, animal words and plural spelling.\nA fact file gives true information: what the animal looks like, where it lives and an amazing fact.\n✔ has for one animal, have for many\n✔ adjective + noun: sharp eyes\n✔ correct plurals: falcons, mice, butterflies\n✔ capital letters and periods","examples":["The falcon has sharp eyes.","Falcons have strong wings.","A falcon doesn't have teeth.","Does a falcon have a long tail? – No, it doesn't.","Falcons eat mice and small birds.","The baby falcons are tiny.","Desert foxes have big ears.","Camels have long eyelashes."],"common_errors":["✗ The falcon have strong wings. → ✓ The falcon has strong wings. (One falcon → has.)","✗ It has eyes sharp. → ✓ It has sharp eyes. (Adjective before the noun.)","✗ Falcons eat mouses. → ✓ Falcons eat mice. (Special plural.)"],"arabic":"نراجع في هذا الدرس have/has والصفات وكلمات الحيوانات والجمع.\nتذكّر: الصفة قبل الاسم، وhas للمفرد وhave للجمع.\nملف الحقائق يذكر شكل الحيوان ومكان عيشه ومعلومة مدهشة عنه."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Animal Fact File: Language in Use”. Let’s learn have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U4-LS5 | Animal Fact File: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Animal interview: one student is an animal. Classmates ask \"Do you have fur? Do you have wings? Are you big?\" and guess the animal.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: have/has, don't/doesn't have, adjectives before nouns, animal words and plural spelling. A fact file gives true information: what the animal looks like, where it lives and an amazing fact.","on_screen":"✔ has for one animal, have for many • ✔ adjective + noun: sharp eyes • ✔ correct plurals: falcons, mice, butterflies","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The falcon has sharp eyes. Falcons have strong wings. A falcon doesn't have teeth.","on_screen":"The falcon has sharp eyes. / Falcons have strong wings. / A falcon doesn't have teeth.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The falcon have strong wings.” That’s not right. We say: “The falcon has strong wings.” One falcon → has.","on_screen":"✗ The falcon have strong wings.   ✓ The falcon has strong wings.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “It has eyes sharp.”? … Think! … It should be “It has sharp eyes.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe an animal to my class.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe an animal to my class.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع في هذا الدرس have/has والصفات وكلمات الحيوانات والجمع.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The falcon have strong wings. — الصحيح: The falcon has strong wings.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف حيوانًا لزملائي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam","body":"The falcon is a beautiful bird. It has strong wings and sharp eyes.\nIt has a short, curved beak.\nFalcons live in deserts and mountains.\nThey are very fast. They can fly faster than a car!\nFalcons are special birds in Saudi Arabia.","word_count":43,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's fact file. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The falcon has strong wings.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The falcon has a long, straight beak.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Falcons live in deserts and mountains.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Falcons are very slow birds.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A falcon can fly faster than a car.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Falcons are not special in Saudi Arabia.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fact File: The Arabian Falcon – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"An owl ___ big round eyes.","options":["is","are","have","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"One animal → has; many animals → have.","explanation_ar":"المفرد has والجمع have."},{"q":"Owls ___ teeth.","options":["not have","don't has","doesn't have","don't have"],"answer":"don't have","explanation":"he/she/it → doesn't have; I/you/we/they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"doesn't مع المفرد الغائب وdon't مع البقية."},{"q":"The fox has ___.","options":["big ears","ears big","big ear","bigs ears"],"answer":"big ears","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"q":"There are many ___ in the garden.","options":["butterflyes","butterflies","butterfly","butterflys"],"answer":"butterflies","explanation":"Check the plural spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الجمع."},{"q":"A ___ has a hump.","options":["rabbit","parrot","camel","turtle"],"answer":"camel","explanation":"Choose the right animal word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الحيوان الصحيحة."},{"q":"My uncle ___ a camel.","options":["has","have","are","is"],"answer":"has","explanation":"One animal → has; many animals → have.","explanation_ar":"المفرد has والجمع have."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Animal interview. Ask and write the answers.","items":[{"q":"Ask: \"Do you have fur?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I do. I have soft fur.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Do you have wings?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"No, I don't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Are you big or small?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"I am small.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Do you have a long tail?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I do.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Guess the animal. Write your guess.","options":[],"answer":"You are a rabbit!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your animal fact file.","items":[{"q":"Plan: choose an animal and write notes – body, home, amazing fact.","options":[],"answer":"camel – hump, long legs; desert; can drink a lot of water","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your fact file in 4–6 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"The camel is a desert animal. It has a big hump. It has long legs. Camels live in the desert. They can drink a lot of water at once.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: has/have? adjectives? plurals? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"camels has\" to \"camels have\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"camel","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lion","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"elephant","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"giraffe","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"rabbit","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"turtle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"parrot","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tail","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wing","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"fur","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"neck","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"shell","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A crab ___ a hard shell.","options":["is","has","have","are"],"answer":"has","explanation":"One animal → has; many animals → have.","explanation_ar":"المفرد has والجمع have."},{"q":"","options":["A snake doesn't have legs.","A snake not have legs.","A snake don't have legs.","A snake doesn't has legs."],"answer":"A snake doesn't have legs.","explanation":"he/she/it → doesn't have; I/you/we/they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"doesn't مع المفرد الغائب وdon't مع البقية."},{"q":"","options":["We see two elephants huge.","We sees two huge elephants.","We see two huges elephants.","We see two huge elephants."],"answer":"We see two huge elephants.","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم."},{"q":"one baby → two ___","options":["baby","babys","babies","babyes"],"answer":"babies","explanation":"Check the plural spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الجمع."},{"q":"This animal has a long neck and eats leaves.","options":["owl","giraffe","crab","mouse"],"answer":"giraffe","explanation":"Choose the right animal word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الحيوان الصحيحة."},{"q":"___ your cat have long fur?","options":["Is","Does","Do","Has"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"he/she/it → doesn't have; I/you/we/they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"doesn't مع المفرد الغائب وdon't مع البقية."},{"q":"Lions ___ big teeth.","options":["have","am","has","is"],"answer":"have","explanation":"One animal → has; many animals → have.","explanation_ar":"المفرد has والجمع have."},{"q":"","options":["The farm has five sheep.","The farm have five sheep.","The farm has five sheeps.","The farm has five sheepes."],"answer":"The farm has five sheep.","explanation":"Check the plural spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الجمع."},{"q":"A bird flies with its ___.","options":["fur","trunk","shell","wings"],"answer":"wings","explanation":"Choose the right animal word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الحيوان الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["Does a turtle has a shell? – Yes, it has.","Do a turtle have a shell? – Yes, it does.","Does a turtle have a shell? – Yes, it does.","Does a turtle have a shell? – Yes, it do."],"answer":"Does a turtle have a shell? – Yes, it does.","explanation":"he/she/it → doesn't have; I/you/we/they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"doesn't مع المفرد الغائب وdon't مع البقية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Adam standing next to a poster titled with a falcon picture, pointing at its wings while classmates take notes. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam standing next to a poster titled with a falcon picture, pointing at its wings while classmates take notes"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Amazing Animals”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Amazing Animals”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS5-T1","script":"The falcon is a beautiful bird. It has strong wings and sharp eyes. It has a short, curved beak. Falcons live in deserts and mountains. They are very fast. They can fly faster than a car! Falcons are special birds in Saudi Arabia.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Animal Fact File: Language in Use”. Let’s learn have/has, adjectives, animal words and plural spelling (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Animal interview: one student is an animal. Classmates ask \"Do you have fur? Do you have wings? Are you big?\" and guess the animal. Today you use all of Unit 4: have/has, don't/doesn't have, adjectives before nouns, animal words and plural spelling. A fact file gives true information: what the animal looks like, where it lives and an amazing fact. Here are some examples. The falcon has sharp eyes. Falcons have strong wings. A falcon doesn't have teeth. Be careful! Some learners say: “The falcon have strong wings.” That’s not right. We say: “The falcon has strong wings.” One falcon → has. Quick check: what is wrong with “It has eyes sharp.”? … Think! … It should be “It has sharp eyes.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe an animal to my class.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"A giraffe ___ a long tongue.","options":["are","is","have","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"We ___ two cats at home.","options":["is","have","has","are"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"My cousin ___ a parrot.","options":["have","are","has","am"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"Ducks ___ orange feet.","options":["have","is","am","has"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"","options":["A camel has a hump.","A camel have a hump.","Camel has a hump.","A camel is a hump."],"answer":"A camel has a hump.","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"A jellyfish ___ bones.","options":["don't have","doesn't has","doesn't have","not has"],"answer":"doesn't have","explanation":"he, she, it → doesn't have (not has).","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't have."},{"q":"___ you have a hamster?","options":["Has","Does","Are","Do"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"Does a lion have a mane? – Yes, it ___.","options":["has","does","do","is"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."},{"q":"","options":["I doesn't have a dog.","I don't has a dog.","I don't have a dog.","I not have a dog."],"answer":"I don't have a dog.","explanation":"I, you, we, they → don't have.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't have."},{"q":"","options":["It has shorts brown fur.","It has short brown fur.","It have short brown fur.","It has fur short brown."],"answer":"It has short brown fur.","explanation":"The adjective comes before the noun and never takes -s.","explanation_ar":"الصفة قبل الاسم ولا تُجمع."},{"q":"An ant is ___.","options":["heavy","tiny","tall","huge"],"answer":"tiny","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A whale is ___.","options":["huge","small","tiny","short"],"answer":"huge","explanation":"tiny < small < big < huge.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الحجم: tiny ثم small ثم big ثم huge."},{"q":"A parrot flies with its ___.","options":["wings","shell","fur","trunk"],"answer":"wings","explanation":"Think about the body part the animal really has.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في جزء الجسم الصحيح للحيوان."},{"q":"This animal has a hard shell and moves slowly.","options":["lion","giraffe","turtle","parrot"],"answer":"turtle","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."},{"q":"The ___ has a big golden mane.","options":["lion","camel","rabbit","turtle"],"answer":"lion","explanation":"Choose the animal that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر الحيوان المناسب للوصف."},{"q":"","options":["The tiger is huge.","The tiger is huges.","The tiger is very huge.","The tiger huge is."],"answer":"The tiger is huge.","explanation":"Don't use very with huge or tiny.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم very مع huge أو tiny."},{"q":"one fox → three ___","options":["fox","foxes","foxs","foxies"],"answer":"foxes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx نضيف es."},{"q":"one puppy → two ___","options":["puppy","puppyes","puppys","puppies"],"answer":"puppies","explanation":"Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى ies."},{"q":"one mouse → five ___","options":["mousies","mices","mouses","mice"],"answer":"mice","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"","options":["I can see four sheeps.","I can see four sheep.","I can see four sheepies.","I can see four sheepes."],"answer":"I can see four sheep.","explanation":"Special plural – learn it by heart.","explanation_ar":"جمع خاص يُحفظ."},{"q":"one turkey → two ___","options":["turkies","turkey","turkeyes","turkeys"],"answer":"turkeys","explanation":"Vowel + y → just add -s (monkeys).","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y نضيف s فقط."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a fact file:","options":["Elephants have ears big.","Elephants has big ears.","Elephants have big ears.","Elephant have big ears."],"answer":"Elephants have big ears.","explanation":"Use have with I, you, we, they and plurals.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم have مع I وyou وwe وthey والجمع."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the parrot have red feathers\"","options":["The parrot has feathers red.","the parrot has red feathers.","The parrot has red feathers.","The parrot have red feathers."],"answer":"The parrot has red feathers.","explanation":"Use has with he, she, it and one person or animal.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم has مع he وshe وit والمفرد."},{"q":"Does your brother have a bike? – ___","options":["No, he don't.","No, he hasn't.","No, he isn't.","No, he doesn't."],"answer":"No, he doesn't.","explanation":"Questions: Do you/they have…? Does he/she/it have…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Do أو Does ثم have."}],"theme_ar":"حيوانات مدهشة","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل كل حيوان مميزًا؟","can_do":"I can describe animals with have/has and adjectives, and spell animal plurals.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف الحيوانات باستخدام have/has والصفات، وأتهجّى جمع أسماء الحيوانات."});
